config.gloamingforest.disable_uncrafting=Disable Uncrafting
config.gloamingforest.disable_uncrafting.tooltip=Disables the uncrafting function of the uncrafting table. Recommended as a last resort if there's too many things to change about its behavior (or you're just lazy, I dont judge).~LINEBREAK~Do note that special uncrafting recipes are not disabled as the mod relies on them for other things.
config.gloamingforest.disable_uncrafting_table=Disable Uncrafting Table
config.gloamingforest.disable_uncrafting_table.tooltip=Disables any usage of the uncrafting table, as well as prevents it from showing up in loot or crafted.~LINEBREAK~Please note that table has more uses than just uncrafting, you can read about them here!~LINEBREAK~It is highly recommended to keep the table enabled as the mod has special uncrafting exclusive recipes, but the option remains for people that dont want the table to be functional at all.~LINEBREAK~If you are looking to just prevent normal crafting recipes from being reversed, consider using the 'disableUncrafting' option instead.
config.gloamingforest.ingredient_switching=Disable Ingredient Switching
config.gloamingforest.ingredient_switching.tooltip=If true, the uncrafting table will no longer allow you to switch between ingredients if a recipe uses a tag for crafting.~LINEBREAK~This will remove the functionality for ALL RECIPES!~LINEBREAK~If you want to prevent certain ingredients from showing up in the first place, use the "gloamingforest:banned_uncrafting_ingredients" tag.
config.gloamingforest.repairing_xp_cost=Repairing Cost Multiplier
config.gloamingforest.repairing_xp_cost.tooltip=Multiplies the total XP cost of repairing an item and rounds up.~LINEBREAK~Higher values means the recipe will cost more to repair, lower means less. Set to 0 to disable the cost altogether.
config.gloamingforest.shapeless_uncrafting=Shapeless Uncrafting
config.gloamingforest.shapeless_uncrafting.tooltip=If true, the uncrafting table will also be allowed to uncraft shapeless recipes.~LINEBREAK~The table was originally intended to only take shaped recipes, but this option remains for people who wish to keep the functionality.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting=Uncrafting Table
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting.tooltip=Settings for all things related to the Uncrafting Table.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_mod_id_flip=Mod ID Blacklist
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_mod_id_flip.tooltip=If true, this will invert the above option from a blacklist to a whitelist.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_mod_ids=Disabled Mod IDs
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_mod_ids.tooltip=Here, you can disable all items from certain mods from being uncrafted.~LINEBREAK~Input a valid mod id to disable all uncrafting recipes from that mod.~LINEBREAK~Example: "gloamingforest" will disable all uncrafting recipes from this mod.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_recipes=Disabled Recipes
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_recipes.tooltip=If you don't want to disable uncrafting altogether, and would rather disable certain recipes, this is for you.~LINEBREAK~To add a recipe, add the mod id followed by the name of the recipe. You can check this in things like JEI.~LINEBREAK~Example: "gloamingforest:firefly_particle_spawner" will disable uncrafting the particle spawner into a firefly jar, firefly, and poppy.~LINEBREAK~If an item has multiple crafting recipes and you wish to disable them all, add the item to the "gloamingforest:banned_uncraftables" item tag.~LINEBREAK~If you have a problematic ingredient, like infested towerwood for example, add the item to the "gloamingforest:banned_uncrafting_ingredients" item tag.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_recipes_flip=Recipe Blacklist
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_recipes_flip.tooltip=If true, this will invert the above uncrafting recipe list from a blacklist to a whitelist.
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_xp_cost=Uncrafting Cost Multiplier
config.gloamingforest.uncrafting_xp_cost.tooltip=Multiplies the total XP cost of uncrafting an item and rounds up.~LINEBREAK~Higher values means the recipe will cost more to uncraft, lower means less. Set to 0 to disable the cost altogether.~LINEBREAK~Note that this only affects reversed crafting recipes, uncrafting recipes will still use the same cost as they normally would.
